             <h2>4. AI Processing</h2>
             <p>To generate exercises and draft feedback, we send the relevant text (for example the exercise or your homework, your level and language) to AI providers acting as our processors: Google (Gemini), Anthropic and Groq. We do not sell this content, and we instruct our providers not to use it to train their models where their services allow it. [COPY NEEDED: confirm that the AI keys used in production are on paid plans whose terms exclude training on customer content.]</p>
             <p>We do not make decisions based solely on automated processing that produce legal or similarly significant effects on you. Homework grades drafted by AI are reviewed and sent by your teacher, and automated practice scores do not affect your account, billing or access. You may ask a person to review any automated result by contacting us.</p>
+            <p>The practice tutor in the student dashboard works the same way. What you write or say in a tutor session is sent to Groq, with your level, the language you learn and a short summary of your learning on Alimun, to produce the tutor's replies. When you speak to the tutor, your recording is sent to Groq to be turned into text and is then discarded; we never store recordings. The tutor's replies are turned into speech by Google Cloud. Tutor conversations are kept for 90 days; session summaries and what the tutor remembers about you are kept until you delete them on the Tutor page or close your account. [COPY NEEDED: legal review of this paragraph, including Google Cloud as a processor and the transfers to Groq and Google Cloud.]</p>
           </div>
 
